{{!--
	The onboarding dialog. NOT an invite dialog -- it has no token, no accept
	and no decline, deliberately.

	It is rendered by Communities.startOnboarding(), which now runs off
	Streams.onInviteResolved, so it appears after the person has accepted or
	declined, and also on a plain login with no invite involved at all.

	communityId is the community of the stream they were invited to, resolved
	server-side from the stream's communityId attribute (falling back to the
	publisher when the publisher is itself a community) -- so being invited
	into a new community re-runs onboarding for THAT community, even for a
	user whose profile is otherwise complete.
--}}
<div id="Communities_onboarding_overlay" class="Communities_onboarding_overlay">
	<div class="Q_title_slot">
		<h2 class="Users_dialog_title Q_dialog_title">{{interpolate onboarding.Title communityName=communityName}}</h2>
	</div>
	<div class="Q_dialog_slot Q_dialog_content">
		{{{tool "Communities/onboarding" communityId=communityId explanation=explanation}}}
	</div>
</div>
